\subsection{Depth matching}\label{sec:S5.4}

Depth is the route of head size that the sphere describes (Section~\ref{sec:S2}). The cortex of the << F.g3b_infant2yr_age_months >>- and << F.g3b_infant12mo_age_months >>-month templates is shallower than the adult's. Their area-weighted median depths were << F.g3b_infant2yr_depth_wmedian >> and << F.g3b_infant12mo_depth_wmedian >> mm, against << F.g3b_adult_depth_wmedian >> mm, and << F.g3b_infant2yr_area_share_10_20mm_pct >> and << F.g3b_infant12mo_area_share_10_20mm_pct >> of their cortical area lay << F.g3b_depth_span_10_20_mm >> mm below the scalp, against << F.g3b_adult_area_share_10_20mm_pct >> in the adult. In the << F.g3b_infant18mo_age_months >>-month template these were << F.g3b_infant18mo_depth_wmedian >> mm and << F.g3b_infant18mo_area_share_10_20mm_pct >>, and in the children << F.g3b_children_depth_wmedian_range >> mm and << F.g3b_children_area_share_10_20mm_pct_range >>. Reweighting each head's targets to the adult's depth distribution lowered the difference of pooled medians from the adult in the fixed helmet. It fell from << F.g3b_infant2yr_pooled_diff >> and << F.g3b_infant12mo_pooled_diff >> to << F.g3b_infant2yr_reweighted_diff >> and << F.g3b_infant12mo_reweighted_diff >> dB in these two templates and from << F.g3b_infant18mo_pooled_diff >> to << F.g3b_infant18mo_reweighted_diff >> dB in the << F.g3b_infant18mo_age_months >>-month template. In the children it fell from a range of << F.g3b_children_pooled_diff_range >> dB to one of << F.g3b_children_reweighted_diff_range >> dB.

Within depth strata, $\Delta$ (the difference of the two heads' area-weighted medians) was positive in every stratum of the principal smaller heads (<< F.wr_depth_strata_principal_dense_ib_delta_range >> dB; Fig.~\ref{fig:S7}A). It was also positive in every stratum of the << F.g3b_infant18mo_age_months >>-month template (<< F.wr_depth_strata_infant18mo_dense_ib_delta_range >> dB). For the children (Section~\ref{sec:S10}), it was negative in << F.g3b_children_depth_10_30mm_delta_negative_count >> of the << F.g3b_children_depth_10_30mm_cells_n >> child-strata at << F.g3b_depth_span_10_30_mm >> mm (<< F.g3b_children_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_10_30mm_delta_range >> dB), with no interval above zero (largest lower bound << F.g3b_children_depth_10_30mm_ci_lo_max >> dB). Deeper, it was positive (<< F.g3b_children_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_30_60mm_delta_range >> dB; Fig.~\ref{fig:S7}B). In this decomposition, their shallower cortex matches their fixed-helmet gain. The depths are measured from the scalp used, unverified near the scalp in the children; measured from the MRI boundary, the children's median depths shift as the adult's do (Section~\ref{sec:S4.3}). The decomposition describes the model's surfaces, not a tested mechanism.

In the helmet fitted at the adult's gap, the children's strata were negative throughout the depths that hold most of their cortex. For child A, $\Delta$ was << F.rev_cgap_child_a_fitted_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_10_15mm_delta >>, << F.rev_cgap_child_a_fitted_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_20_25mm_delta >> and << F.rev_cgap_child_a_fitted_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_30_40mm_delta >> dB at << F.wr_cgap_depth_10_15_label >>, << F.wr_cgap_depth_20_25_label >> and << F.wr_cgap_depth_30_40_label >> mm, its intervals including zero only from the << F.wr_cgap_depth_40_50_label >> mm stratum down. The two decompositions, fitting the helmet and matching depth, are not additive, and neither apportions the routes exactly.

