\subsection{Noise in the smaller heads and the share of cortex where the OPM's detectability is higher}\label{sec:S5.5}

With the adult's background variance per unit cortical area in every head, the noise differs between classes of head. In the fixed helmet, Neuromag's magnetometer brain noise fell from << F.g3b_adult_noise_top_mag_brain >> fT in the adult at top contact (<< F.g3b_adult_noise_centred_mag_brain >> fT at its measured pose) to << F.g3b_principal_noise_top_mag_brain_range >> fT in the principal smaller heads. Their wider gap and smaller cortex both contribute, and the shares were not separated: moving the school-age scaled adult from its centered pose to top contact raised this noise from << F.g3b_school_noise_centred_mag_brain >> to << F.g3b_school_noise_top_mag_brain >> fT. A smaller cortex does not lower the field at sensors that stay close, as the OPMs show (<< F.g3b_school_noise_dense_brain >> and << F.g3b_size2yr_noise_dense_brain >> fT in the scaled adults, against << F.g3b_adult_noise_dense_brain >> fT in the adult).

The children's cortex is nearly adult-sized (<< F.g3b_children_cortex_area_cm2_range >> cm²), so Neuromag's brain noise stayed at << F.g3b_children_noise_top_mag_brain_range >> fT. The OPMs, close to a near-adult cortex that lies near the scalp in these surfaces (unverified there; Sections~\ref{sec:S4.3} and \ref{sec:S10.1}), saw more of it (<< F.g3b_children_noise_dense_brain_range >> fT).

The share of cortex on which the OPM's detectability is higher, the kind of metric used by \citet{jas2026}, is saturated for the dense array (<< F.wr_adult_dense_ib_share_pos_pct >> of cortical area in the adult). For the site-matched array it was << F.wr_adult_matched_ib_share_pos_pct >> in the adult at top contact (<< F.g2_matched_vs_combined_ib_share >> of all targets at the measured pose). As a proportion of cortical area in the fixed helmet, it was << F.g3b_principal_matched_vs_combined_ib_d_share_pos_range >> in the principal smaller heads and << F.g3b_provisional_matched_vs_combined_ib_d_share_pos_range >> in the heads of Section~\ref{sec:S10} (Fig.~\ref{fig:S8}C).

